{"weatherAlerts":[{"alertId":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.eb8193b8fbd42ea37824d6a9b67048487fdf921c.001.1","alertTitle":{"text":"Flood Watch","languageCode":"en"},"eventType":"FLOOD","areaName":"Utah","instruction":["You should monitor later forecasts and be prepared to take action\nshould Flash Flood Warnings be issued."],"safetyRecommendations":[{"directive":"Build an emergency kit and make a family communications plan.","subtext":"Follow the instructions at http://www.ready.gov/build-a-kit for building an emergency kit and http://www.ready.gov/make-a-plan for a family communications plan."},{"directive":"Elevate the furnace, water heater and electric panel in your home if you live in an area that has a high flood risk."},{"directive":"Consider installing \"check valves\" to prevent flood water from backing up into the drains of your home."},{"directive":"If feasible, construct barriers to stop floodwater from entering the building and seal walls in basements with waterproofing compounds."},{"directive":"For more information on what to do before a flood, visit http://www.ready.gov/floods?qt-view__field_tabs_view__default__106=0"},{"directive":"Be aware that flash flooding can occur. ","subtext":"If there is any possibility of a flash flood, move immediately to higher ground. Do not wait for instructions to move."},{"directive":"Turn off utilities at the main switches or valves if instructed to do so. Disconnect electrical appliances. Do not touch electrical equipment if you are wet or standing in water.","subtext":"Follow the instructions at https://www.ready.gov/safety-skills."},{"directive":"Secure your home. If you have time, bring in outdoor furniture. Move essential items to an upper floor."},{"directive":"Be aware of stream, drainage channels, canyons and other areas known to flood suddenly.","subtext":"Flash floods can occur in these areas with or without typical warnings such as rain clouds or heavy rain."},{"directive":"Do not walk through moving water. Use a stick to check the firmness of the ground in front of you.","subtext":"Six inches of moving water can make you fall. If you have to walk in water, walk where the water is not moving. "},{"directive":"Do not drive into flooded areas. If floodwaters rise around your car, abandon the car and move to higher ground if you can do so safely.","subtext":"You and the vehicle can be swept away quickly."},{"directive":"Do not camp or park your vehicle along streams, rivers or creeks, particularly during threatening conditions."},{"directive":"For more information on what to do during a flood, visit http://www.ready.gov/floods?qt-view__field_tabs_view__default__106=1"}],"timezoneOffset":"-21600s","dataSource":{"publisher":"NOAA","name":"National Weather Service","authorityUri":"https://www.weather.gov/"},"polygon":"{\"type\":\"MultiPolygon\",\"coordinates\":[[[[-110.062833,38.655373],[-110.050922,38.657494],[-110.062833,38.665443],[-110.062833,38.655373]]],[[[-109.896097,39.793581],[-109.884189,39.785798],[-109.872281,39.797817],[-109.896097,39.793581]]],[[[-110.098567,38.980507],[-110.062833,38.976874],[-110.074744,38.964723],[-110.003279,38.947388],[-110.003279,38.967443],[-110.027100,38.973226],[-110.062833,38.996915],[-110.062833,38.986895],[-110.098567,38.980507]]],[[[-110.181954,37.322595],[-110.158128,37.316552],[-110.122391,37.292072],[-110.086655,37.257288],[-110.062833,37.240929],[-110.039011,37.245118],[-110.039011,37.214275],[-110.015190,37.228740],[-110.003279,37.199976],[-109.991369,37.202063],[-109.979460,37.193861],[-109.967550,37.195946],[-109.967550,37.216520],[-109.943731,37.210399],[-109.943731,37.241256],[-110.003279,37.241111],[-110.003279,37.261670],[-110.039011,37.255396],[-110.039011,37.275948],[-110.050922,37.273854],[-110.074744,37.300476],[-110.098567,37.296276],[-110.098567,37.327077],[-110.181954,37.322595]]],[[[-110.134303,39.084231],[-110.110479,39.128502],[-110.110479,39.158486],[-110.098567,39.180603],[-110.074744,39.214831],[-110.074744,39.2248