79],[-110.146216,38.841585],[-110.134303,38.863796],[-110.146216,38.871697],[-110.158128,38.859526],[-110.158128,38.899659],[-110.181954,38.915438],[-110.158128,38.929743],[-110.134303,38.923988],[-110.146216,38.951928],[-110.146216,38.961950],[-110.146216,38.981989],[-110.122391,38.976242],[-110.122391,38.986261],[-110.110479,38.978375],[-110.098567,38.980507],[-110.098567,39.000545],[-110.134303,39.004159],[-110.146216,39.012037],[-110.146216,39.022049],[-110.158128,39.039931],[-110.134303,39.064222],[-110.146216,39.072089],[-110.146216,39.092095],[-110.134303,39.084231]],[[-110.027100,38.449885],[-110.039011,38.447771],[-110.027100,38.459989],[-110.027100,38.449885]],[[-110.086655,38.671265],[-110.086655,38.661197],[-110.098567,38.669140],[-110.086655,38.671265]],[[-110.134303,39.004159],[-110.146216,38.992006],[-110.146216,39.002022],[-110.134303,39.004159]],[[-110.634771,37.210627],[-110.646690,37.218722],[-110.646690,37.228978],[-110.634771,37.220885],[-110.634771,37.210627]]]]}","description":"FLOOD WATCH REMAINS IN EFFECT THROUGH MONDAY AFTERNOON\n\n* WHAT...Flash flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...A portion of Utah, including the following areas, Castle\nCountry, Central Mountains, Eastern Juab/Millard Counties, San\nRafael Swell, Sanpete Valley, Sevier Valley, Wasatch Plateau/Book\nCliffs, Bryce Canyon Country, Capitol Reef National Park and\nVicinity, Glen Canyon Recreation Area/Lake Powell, South Central\nUtah, Southern Mountains, Upper Sevier River Valleys, Western\nCanyonlands, Lower Washington County, Southwest Utah and Zion\nNational Park. This also includes recent burn scars such as\nForsyth, Cottonwood, Silver King, France Canyon, and Monroe Canyon.\n\n* WHEN...Through Monday afternoon.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, dry washes, slot canyons, and other low-lying and\nflood-prone locations such as slickrock areas and recent burn\nscars. Creeks and streams may rise out of their banks. Flooding may\noccur in poor drainage and urban areas.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n\n- Anomalously high moisture from the remnants of Tropical Storm\nRachel will continue to impact the region. While this is expected\nto be a long duration rainfall event, scattered instances of\nheavier rainfall rates are expected with stronger storms yielding\nflash flooding concerns given saturated soils and prior burn\nscars.\n\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","severity":"SEVERE","certainty":"POSSIBLE","urgency":"FUTURE","startTime":"2026-10-11T12:42:00Z","expirationTime":"2026-10-12T03:45:00Z"},{"alertId":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.92b536704cbd5fed3f025b74d4ff8869d9d615a1.004.1","alertTitle":{"text":"High Wind Warning","languageCode":"en"},"eventType":"WIND","areaName":"Southern Mountains (Utah)","instruction":["Winds this strong can make driving difficult, especially for high\nprofile vehicles and vehicles with trailers. Use extra caution.\n\nPeople are urged to secure loose objects that could be blown around\nor damaged by the wind."],"safetyRecommendations":[],"timezoneOffset":"-21600s","dataSource":{"publisher":"NOAA","name":"National Weather Service","authorityUri":"https://www.weather.gov/"},"polygon":"{\"type\":\"MultiPolygon\",\"coordinates\":[[[[-113.900114,36.995374],[-113.721631,37.002813],[-113.769233,37.104220],[-113.840627,37.220570],[-113.876320,37.223072],[-113.912011,37.245760],[-113.935803,37.230575],[-113.959594,37.164861],[-113.947699,37.086493],[-113.888217,37.058690],[-113.888217,37.018173],[-113.900114,36.995374]]],[[[-110.765887,38.164620],[-110.849331,38.179550],[-110.897016,38.110036],[-110.885095,38.092007],[-110.897016,38.079676],[-110.920859,38.034755],[-110.897016,38.029047],[-110.849331,37.997338],[-110.861252,37.964720],[-110.837410,37.928549],[-110.837410,37.918401],[-110.801648,37.894541],[-110.742046,37.885188],[-110.730126,37.856896],[-110.670528,37.847480],[-110.634771,37.894664],[-110.610933,37.899012],[-110.6