high as 97 mph on Big Mountain south of\nEnterprise, otherwise wind gusts to around 75 mph have been\nobserved near Brian Head.\n\n* WHERE...Southern Mountains.\n\n* WHEN...Until midnight MDT tonight.\n\n* IMPACTS...High winds may move loose debris, damage property and\ncause power outages. Travel could be difficult, especially for high\nprofile vehicles and vehicles with trailers.","severity":"SEVERE","certainty":"LIKELY","urgency":"EXPECTED","startTime":"2026-10-11T16:31:00Z","expirationTime":"2026-10-12T06:00:00Z"},{"alertId":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.70c94b643686dfec9ee3a7bdade8d63778f1c3ad.001.1","alertTitle":{"text":"Flash Flood Warning","languageCode":"en"},"eventType":"FLASH_FLOOD","areaName":"Washington","instruction":["This is a life threatening situation. Heavy rainfall will cause\nextensive and severe flash flooding of creeks...streams...and ditches\nin the Forsyth Burn Scar. Severe debris flows can also be anticipated\nacross roads. Roads and driveways may be washed away in places. If\nyou encounter flood waters...climb to safety.\n\nBe aware of your surroundings and do not drive on flooded roads.\n\nFlooding is occurring or is imminent. It is important to know where\nyou are relative to streams, rivers, or creeks which can become\nkillers in heavy rains. Campers and hikers should avoid streams or\ncreeks."],"safetyRecommendations":[],"timezoneOffset":"-21600s","dataSource":{"publisher":"NOAA","name":"National Weather Service","authorityUri":"https://www.weather.gov/"},"polygon":"{\"type\":\"Polygon\",\"coordinates\":[[[-113.310000,37.440000],[-113.360000,37.510000],[-113.500000,37.480000],[-113.640000,37.430000],[-113.630000,37.310000],[-113.510000,37.260000],[-113.410000,37.270000],[-113.290000,37.380000],[-113.310000,37.440000]]]}","description":"FFWSLC\n\nThe National Weather Service in Salt Lake City has extended the\n\n* Flash Flood Warning for...\nThe Forsyth burn scar in...\nCentral Washington County in southwestern Utah...\n\n* Until 915 PM MDT.\n\n* At 604 PM MDT, Emergency management reported heavy rain over the\nForsyth Burn Scar and flooding in Pine Valley. Additionally, river\ngauges remain high along the Santa Clara River above Baker\nReservoir. Between 1.50 and 3 inches of rain have fallen. Flash\nflooding is ongoing. Excessive rainfall over the burn scar will\nresult in debris flow. The debris flow can consist of rock, mud,\nvegetation and other loose materials.\n\nHAZARD...Life threatening flash flooding. Heavy rain producing\nflash flooding in and around the Forsyth Burn Scar.\n\nSOURCE...Emergency management reported.\n\nIMPACT...Life threatening flash flooding of areas in and around the\nForsyth Burn Scar.\n\n* Some locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nPine Valley.\n\nThis includes Utah Route 18 between mile markers 26 and 27.","severity":"SEVERE","certainty":"LIKELY","urgency":"IMMEDIATE","startTime":"2026-10-12T00:04:00Z","expirationTime":"2026-10-12T03:15:00Z"}],"regionCode":"US","nextPageToken":""}